From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] wineboot, server: the font list key is not volatile (3604)

wineboot, server: the font list can be written again (System and Fixedsys fonts)

Patch 0242 makes wineboot create HKLM\System\CurrentControlSet\Hardware
Profiles\Current\System\... volatile. A volatile create makes every missing
parent volatile, "Current" included, and a volatile key takes no persistent
child. win32u keeps the font list (FONTS.FON, FIXEDFON.FON, OEMFONT.FON) under
Hardware Profiles\Current\Software\Fonts; creating it failed, so the bitmap
System and Fixedsys fonts were never loaded and "System" was drawn with
Tahoma. riched20 uses the System font for its default format, so its text
metrics and scrolling differed from stock Wine (editor.c EM_SCROLL, EM_FORMATRANGE,
richole), and every program asking for the System font got another face.

wineboot now creates the Software\Fonts key first, non-volatile, and the server
gives that key the user-writable DACL of the display configuration keys, so any
program's win32u can write the list as in stock Wine.

Gate: test/fastb-fontkey-gate.sh (mutant: the new create skipped, caught).

Rebased at integration (integ-2026-10) onto 3764 (main): main's 3764 already gives Hardware Profiles\Current\Software\Fonts the user-writable DACL (same server hunk); 3604 keeps only the wineboot non-volatile creation.
---
diff --git a/programs/wineboot/wineboot.c b/programs/wineboot/wineboot.c
--- a/programs/wineboot/wineboot.c
+++ b/programs/wineboot/wineboot.c
@@ -981,6 +981,17 @@ static void create_display_config_keys(void)
     unsigned int i;
     HKEY key;
 
+    /* The font list (FONTS.FON, FIXEDFON.FON: the System and Fixedsys fonts)
+     * is kept by win32u under Hardware Profiles\Current\Software\Fonts and is
+     * not volatile. Created first, so that "Current" is not made volatile
+     * by the volatile keys below (a volatile key takes no persistent child:
+     * the list could not be written, and the System and Fixedsys fonts were
+     * missing). */
+    if (!RegCreateKeyExW( HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE, L"System\\CurrentControlSet\\Hardware Profiles\\Current\\Software\\Fonts",
+                          0, NULL, REG_OPTION_NON_VOLATILE, KEY_ALL_ACCESS, NULL, &key, NULL ))
+        RegCloseKey( key );
+    else WARN( "cannot create the font list key\n" );
+
     for (i = 0; i < ARRAY_SIZE(keys); i++)
     {
         if (RegCreateKeyExW( HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE, keys[i], 0, NULL, REG_OPTION_VOLATILE,
